export abstract anchor FactoryObservability:
    factModel:
        Every fact has a value and an independent state. States are current,
        stale, unknown, and unavailable. A real zero is a value with state
        current, not a state. Precedence is unavailable, unknown, stale, then
        current. Unknown means no reading has ever been obtained; unavailable
        means the source cannot be reached.
        A derived fact inherits the worst state of its required inputs. It is
        withheld only when no value can be produced; withholding is rendered as
        unknown, never as silent omission.
    freshness:
        Policy sets a maximum freshness limit per fact class. A source may
        declare a shorter limit but not a longer one. Each rendered fact shows
        its age, limit, source, policy version, and provenance: observed,
        estimated, projected, reserved, or unresolved exposure. Derived facts
        reference their inputs. A fresh snapshot never upgrades a fact, and a
        stale snapshot floors every fact's freshness.
    healthScopes:
        Health is scoped to factory, account, route, target, and order. Each
        scope has a minimum required fact set: factory covers dispatch, budget,
        queue, and unresolved exposure; account covers usage and reading age;
        route covers breaker and wiring validity; target covers lease and queue;
        order covers step, question, and liveness state.
        A scope is degraded when a required fact is stale, unknown, or
        unavailable. Factory health is degraded when a required global fact is
        bad or when every child scope of a required kind is degraded; otherwise
        it reports a degraded-scope count. Total child failure cannot render
        green.
    readAccess:
        The engineer may read all operational facts. An agent may read its own
        step and attempt records, its order's plan and dependency states, and
        aggregate queue, capacity, and budget facts; it may not read another
        order's prompts, evidence, or artifacts. An auditor may read
        operational facts, evidence references, and audit entries, but not
        secrets, prompts, or artifact content unless separately granted, and
        performs no operation. Dashboard reads pass the same filter as CLI
        reads.
    actionSet:
        The dashboard exposes submit and answer. Onboard, start, and shutdown
        remain CLI and onboarding surfaces. Every exposed action uses the
        standard operation envelope and authorization. A read-only deployment
        declares no actions and is not treated as degraded runtime mode.
        Degraded runtime mode keeps status, answer, and shutdown available for
        repair.
    observabilityConformance:
        Separately verdicted cells inject a fresh control and a fault on the
        same fact: fresh usage, stale usage, unreachable usage source, real
        zero, unknown model availability, and missing queue data. Each asserts
        the value, state, age, limit, policy version, source, and reason cause.
        Health cells assert order-local degradation without global red, global
        degradation from a global required fact, all-child failure rendering
        degraded, and recovery to current.
        Access cells assert an authorized engineer action, a rejected
        unauthorized action with no state change, an agent reading only its own
        order facts, an auditor reading facts but not secrets or prompts and
        performing no action, and a read-only deployment exposing no actions.
        Parity cells inject a source update and require both surfaces to show
        it, and run submit and answer through each surface with exactly one
        effect. A cell that never reaches its condition is not passed;
        not-applicable is not a pass except for a declared read-only deployment
        with its own evidence.
